WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:37.017
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:37.287 --> 00:40.666
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

3
00:48.674 --> 00:51.385
Don't you think Prince Heinrey is so dashing?

4
01:20.998 --> 01:23.875
Your Highness, I heard that you've searched ardently.

5
01:24.793 --> 01:27.254
I am the secret pen pal you've been writing to.

6
01:28.922 --> 01:31.341
Your "lost fate", and you found me now.

7
02:05.625 --> 02:06.793
So, you say…

8
02:07.586 --> 02:08.878
you're my correspondent?

9
02:08.879 --> 02:10.464
Yes.

10
02:13.508 --> 02:14.676
Prove it to me.

11
02:18.597 --> 02:20.641
You're suspicious, aren't you?

12
02:22.017 --> 02:24.143
Yes, with good reason too.

13
02:24.144 --> 02:26.605
This is someone who is very precious to me.

14
02:30.484 --> 02:33.362
If you really are that person, I would be happy.

15
02:34.821 --> 02:36.531
But if you are not that person,

16
02:37.449 --> 02:39.868
there would be consequences for disappointing me.

17
02:40.827 --> 02:42.704
What exactly might you do?

18
02:47.751 --> 02:48.752
Who can say?

19
02:49.920 --> 02:51.338
Do not think about that.

20
02:51.838 --> 02:54.257
That will never occur with us in any case.

21
02:57.344 --> 03:00.012
Since I shall prove to you that I was indeed

22
03:00.013 --> 03:01.598
behind those letters.

23
03:03.600 --> 03:06.352
Only we know the bird is our messenger.

24
03:06.353 --> 03:07.646
That is a secret.

25
03:09.064 --> 03:10.482
It is only me

26
03:11.149 --> 03:12.692
and you, the prince,

27
03:12.693 --> 03:14.361
who know the bird has a name.

28
03:15.195 --> 03:16.613
What is the bird's name?

29
03:18.657 --> 03:19.658
It is Queen.

30
03:20.909 --> 03:23.536
That bird's noble feathers appealed to me,

31
03:23.537 --> 03:26.247
so Rashta was the one who personally named it.

32
03:26.248 --> 03:27.541
Queen.

33
03:38.885 --> 03:40.095
The name is correct.

34
03:41.972 --> 03:43.055
Queen.

35
04:11.293 --> 04:13.085
Where is Queen now?

36
04:13.086 --> 04:15.755
I'm sure he's near you.

37
04:18.341 --> 04:21.595
Queen! Where are you?

38
04:22.387 --> 04:23.889
Come out and see us!

39
04:24.431 --> 04:26.474
Rashta is here!

40
04:26.475 --> 04:28.268
Come on out here!

41
04:29.144 --> 04:30.478
Queen!

42
04:30.479 --> 04:31.730
Where are you?

43
04:32.606 --> 04:34.274
Come out and see me!

44
04:41.823 --> 04:44.950
I did not wish to offend. I had to confirm it was you.

45
04:44.951 --> 04:47.496
You were seeking someone who's very dear to you.

46
04:49.080 --> 04:53.918
It took much courage for Rashta, who is the Emperor's woman,

47
04:53.919 --> 04:56.296
to seek you out while everyone is watching.

48
04:59.049 --> 05:00.133
I've waited for this.

49
05:02.427 --> 05:04.137
I wanted very much for us to meet.

50
05:22.989 --> 05:26.075
That sly fox. She has no shame, does she?

51
05:26.076 --> 05:27.451
It's that Rashta again.

52
05:27.452 --> 05:28.702
She's claiming that she's the one

53
05:28.703 --> 05:31.248
who is exchanging secret letters with Prince Heinrey.

54
05:32.082 --> 05:33.165
Oh goodness.

55
05:33.166 --> 05:35.709
Your Majesty, only you can put this right.

56
05:35.710 --> 05:38.504
You should expose her lies and humiliate her so thoroughly

57
05:38.505 --> 05:40.923
that she won't be able to show her face again.

58
05:43.343 --> 05:44.636
There's more to this.

59
05:46.263 --> 05:48.765
The content of those letters was private and personal.

60
05:51.351 --> 05:52.853
So how could Rashta know it?

61
06:01.486 --> 06:02.862
My apologies.

62
06:02.863 --> 06:04.780
I will bring the source to light

63
06:04.781 --> 06:06.490
and punish the spy.

64
06:06.491 --> 06:08.118
I shall restore discipline, my lady.

65
06:11.037 --> 06:13.123
Ah!

66
06:14.165 --> 06:15.291
- This way! - Where are you?

67
06:15.292 --> 06:16.625
- Where? - I'm here!

68
06:16.626 --> 06:18.837
- Here? - Here, over here!

69
06:19.421 --> 06:21.213
- Go on, yes! - Where are you?

70
06:21.214 --> 06:22.423
Aw! He moved!

71
06:22.424 --> 06:24.550
- Quick, she's coming for us! - Where are you? Here?

72
06:26.553 --> 06:27.804
Oh! Oh.

73
06:28.680 --> 06:29.681
Oh.

74
06:30.932 --> 06:32.225
Are you hurt?

75
06:33.268 --> 06:34.352
Your hand.

76
06:38.815 --> 06:40.107
There! I beat you!

77
06:40.108 --> 06:42.484
Get up.

78
06:42.485 --> 06:44.987
Here, I'll help you.

79
06:44.988 --> 06:46.531
I beat you!

80
06:47.324 --> 06:48.699
I caught you.

81
06:51.578 --> 06:53.621
- Where are you going? - Come over here!

82
06:53.622 --> 06:55.456
Come around it! Come this way!

83
06:55.457 --> 06:56.957
Careful!

84
06:56.958 --> 06:59.168
"I beat you."

85
06:59.169 --> 07:00.669
- This way! - Here we are!

86
07:00.670 --> 07:01.920
Go on, get her!

87
07:09.304 --> 07:10.387
How's this?

88
07:10.388 --> 07:11.847
You'd look so beautiful, as always.

89
07:11.848 --> 07:13.725
Ms. Rashta!

90
07:15.602 --> 07:18.229
Just look how many invitations people have sent you!

91
07:22.150 --> 07:24.943
I think everyone is talking about you today.

92
07:24.944 --> 07:27.571
They are all saying that there's no competition,

93
07:27.572 --> 07:29.990
and there's no one as dazzling as you this New Year!

94
07:31.117 --> 07:33.702
Our banquet needs a larger venue. Don't you think?

95
07:33.703 --> 07:34.787
Absolutely.

96
07:34.788 --> 07:36.664
More than 100 people will come.

97
07:36.665 --> 07:38.500
Well, I must tell Lady Albani, then.

98
07:40.251 --> 07:41.919
Throw these away.

99
07:41.920 --> 07:44.296
They're just petty gatherings.

100
07:44.297 --> 07:46.674
I'll be far too busy with all the important parties.

101
07:46.675 --> 07:47.925
Of course.

102
07:47.926 --> 07:48.927
Ah.

103
07:49.761 --> 07:51.845
Can you please tell us about Prince Heinrey?

104
07:51.846 --> 07:54.431
- He seems lovely. - You two look so wonderful together.

105
07:54.432 --> 07:56.392
- It's true! - Really?

106
07:56.393 --> 07:58.186
Given what's happened…

107
07:59.187 --> 08:01.356
I think you should take him as a lover.

108
08:02.691 --> 08:06.569
Can the Emperor's lady make a conquest of her own?

109
08:08.154 --> 08:10.239
More to the point, who would know?

110
08:16.913 --> 08:20.207
What should we do with the present that came with the invitation?

111
08:20.208 --> 08:21.459
A present, you say?

112
08:24.796 --> 08:27.089
- Ta-da! - It's a beautiful carpet!

113
08:28.258 --> 08:29.509
But where are the jewels?

114
08:30.218 --> 08:31.760
It looks expensive.

115
08:31.761 --> 08:34.389
And a real high-quality item for sure.

116
08:35.098 --> 08:37.391
- You have it. - Mmm. Me?

117
08:37.392 --> 08:41.437
I would say you deserve a reward for all your hard work with the letters.

118
08:41.438 --> 08:42.771
Oh!

119
08:42.772 --> 08:44.440
Thank you, Ms. Rashta, truly!

120
08:44.441 --> 08:46.025
In return,

121
08:46.026 --> 08:47.819
you must find out even more now.

122
08:48.403 --> 08:50.237
I want to know everything that's written.

123
08:50.238 --> 08:53.323
Also, bring any information on the Empress' life.

124
08:53.324 --> 08:54.701
But stay discreet.

125
08:55.994 --> 08:58.370
Kisia, the same goes for you.

126
08:58.371 --> 08:59.664
Hear this.

127
09:01.332 --> 09:02.791
Stay faithful to me.

128
09:02.792 --> 09:05.335
I'll be even more generous if you stay loyal.

129
09:05.336 --> 09:06.795
Yes, I will, Ms. Rashta.

130
09:09.090 --> 09:10.216
Majesty!

131
09:15.513 --> 09:17.724
Mmm. I missed you so much.

132
09:18.475 --> 09:21.102
You have something to say?

133
09:22.479 --> 09:25.607
You've been listening to the rumors, then? Have you?

134
09:28.234 --> 09:30.736
I tried to tell you about it first, Your Majesty.

135
09:30.737 --> 09:33.364
I did go to your palace yesterday.

136
09:33.948 --> 09:35.158
And again this morning.

137
09:38.912 --> 09:42.916
Everyone in the palace prefers talking to Her Majesty the Empress.

138
09:43.541 --> 09:45.501
Rashta was feeling lonely.

139
09:45.502 --> 09:48.504
Nobody wants anything to do with Rashta.

140
09:48.505 --> 09:50.089
I just wanted a friend.

141
09:50.090 --> 09:52.175
It was nice even just by letter.

142
09:55.428 --> 09:57.346
With a foreign royal?

143
09:57.347 --> 10:00.182
But I would have preferred it much, much more

144
10:00.183 --> 10:01.351
to spend time with you.

145
10:04.813 --> 10:06.313
Well, then,

146
10:06.314 --> 10:09.399
did those blasted letters bring you some comfort

147
10:09.400 --> 10:11.069
in your lonely palace life?

148
10:11.736 --> 10:13.195
You're all I need.

149
10:13.196 --> 10:14.823
My comfort is you, Your Majesty.

150
10:17.242 --> 10:19.576
Your Majesty is my sunshine

151
10:19.577 --> 10:20.787
and my big joy…

152
10:21.412 --> 10:22.831
and salvation.

153
10:25.041 --> 10:26.292
Oh!

154
10:28.378 --> 10:29.587
Cute.

155
10:31.131 --> 10:32.132
Cute as can be.

156
10:32.882 --> 10:35.301
You're even more cute when you're sulking.

157
10:35.927 --> 10:38.012
Cute when you're being jealous.

158
10:39.305 --> 10:41.431
The cutest man.

159
10:41.432 --> 10:43.559
Rashta has one request.

160
10:43.560 --> 10:45.979
I have heard there's another banquet arranged.

161
10:46.646 --> 10:48.438
Rashta would like you to bring her, please.

162
10:48.439 --> 10:49.731
Since this one is special,

163
10:49.732 --> 10:52.235
and all the most important people will be there.

164
10:52.735 --> 10:54.027
If you know all of that,

165
10:54.028 --> 10:56.405
then you should also know that you're not allowed to attend.

166
10:56.406 --> 10:58.031
If you take me,

167
10:58.032 --> 11:00.951
I won't be forced to ask Prince Heinrey to take me instead.

168
11:02.412 --> 11:03.955
Aw!

169
11:05.123 --> 11:06.791
Please take me with you. Mm.

170
11:10.253 --> 11:13.213
They are calling it "The rediscovery of Ms. Rashta."

171
11:13.214 --> 11:14.882
Her commoner-like cheerfulness.

172
11:14.883 --> 11:17.594
And, of course, the praise for her looks goes without saying!

173
11:18.303 --> 11:19.678
What else did they say?

174
11:19.679 --> 11:23.432
"She's as innocent as a baby and a total angel."

175
11:23.433 --> 11:25.560
Ha! What a joke.

176
11:28.313 --> 11:30.439
So, why on earth are you letting her fool you?

177
11:30.440 --> 11:31.565
What is it?

178
11:31.566 --> 11:33.483
Why are you doing this?

179
11:33.484 --> 11:35.777
Her blatant lies haven't pushed you over the edge?

180
11:35.778 --> 11:37.738
It's party to party with her on your arm.

181
11:37.739 --> 11:41.158
Why are you escorting her around and raising her value like that?

182
11:41.159 --> 11:43.911
- Her happiness, that's why. - What?

183
11:43.912 --> 11:46.998
I'll indulge her and let her prance around to her heart's content.

184
11:48.208 --> 11:52.420
Then my next move, when she is perfectly at ease…

185
12:02.430 --> 12:04.431
You are such a sly, devious person.

186
12:04.432 --> 12:05.642
Are you aware of that?

187
12:06.768 --> 12:08.602
I very clearly warned that woman.

188
12:08.603 --> 12:10.187
Enough is enough.

189
12:10.188 --> 12:12.940
I told her if she lied, my anger would be severe.

190
12:12.941 --> 12:14.567
She has to pay the price.

191
12:17.779 --> 12:19.238
The price

192
12:19.239 --> 12:21.491
for exploiting a prince to grow her status.

193
12:24.786 --> 12:25.912
The price…

194
12:26.371 --> 12:28.456
for daring to act the "Queen".

195
12:36.714 --> 12:38.215
What is the order of entrance?

196
12:38.216 --> 12:39.758
Grand Duke Kaufman of Luipt,

197
12:39.759 --> 12:42.469
Princess Circe, Prince Heinrey of the Western Kingdom,

198
12:42.470 --> 12:44.304
then Grand Prince Sirim of Bohemia.

199
12:44.305 --> 12:46.056
The Grand Duke will be in blue-green,

200
12:46.057 --> 12:48.141
Prince Heinrey will be dressed in white,

201
12:48.142 --> 12:50.143
and Emperor Sovieshu in black.

202
12:50.144 --> 12:53.189
Shall we prepare black for you as well, to match His Majesty?

203
12:55.650 --> 12:58.861
Could I select something for you to wear?

204
13:00.905 --> 13:02.490
Simple and elegant.

205
13:30.977 --> 13:35.315
Her Majesty the Empress, Navier Ellie Trovi, is entering.

206
13:39.902 --> 13:44.322
The bird was just so lovely, and that's why I named it Queen.

207
13:44.323 --> 13:46.242
Really?

208
13:47.076 --> 13:48.201
Sist…

209
13:48.202 --> 13:49.203
Ah.

210
13:50.413 --> 13:52.248
Your Majesty.

211
14:02.675 --> 14:04.385
Your Majesty, you've come at last.

212
14:12.143 --> 14:14.019
"Sister"?

213
14:14.020 --> 14:15.063
Uh…

214
14:16.105 --> 14:17.773
You know what I really think?

215
14:17.774 --> 14:20.358
She's far too old to be my big sister.

216
14:23.696 --> 14:26.491
It's an honor to be seated next to you, Your Majesty.

217
14:30.912 --> 14:32.370
Were you surprised?

218
14:32.371 --> 14:34.414
Actually, I'm impressed.

219
14:34.415 --> 14:37.042
I had thought I would be the most stylish…

220
14:37.043 --> 14:38.878
and then I saw you, Princess Circe.

221
14:39.962 --> 14:43.590
I'm afraid Grand Duke Kaufman won't even meet my eyes

222
14:43.591 --> 14:45.258
because of what I'm wearing.

223
14:45.259 --> 14:49.262
In Luipt, it is considered extremely rude for a lady to wear trousers.

224
14:49.263 --> 14:51.723
It's seen to be an act of great disrespect.

225
14:51.724 --> 14:53.266
I wear trousers when hunting.

226
14:53.267 --> 14:54.392
They're comfortable.

227
14:54.393 --> 14:56.561
Customs vary between kingdoms.

228
14:56.562 --> 14:58.063
What on earth is wisteria?

229
15:01.818 --> 15:04.778
In my country, if a man's lover ever approached his wife,

230
15:04.779 --> 15:06.905
she would be executed immediately.

231
15:26.717 --> 15:29.803
Ms. Rashta's new necklace is perfectly beautiful.

232
15:29.804 --> 15:33.015
I heard it was a gift from you, Your Majesty.

233
15:34.058 --> 15:35.268
Really?

234
15:37.979 --> 15:40.564
Yes. Ms. Rashta told us so.

235
15:40.565 --> 15:43.651
That you sent it as a gift to mark her entering the palace.

236
15:44.777 --> 15:47.655
That Your Majesty cares for and cherishes her like family.

237
15:51.951 --> 15:53.076
She's mistaken.

238
15:53.077 --> 15:54.995
I did not send her anything.

239
15:54.996 --> 15:56.955
- Ms. Rashta is confused. - Ah…

240
15:56.956 --> 15:58.748
This is surely a misunderstanding.

241
15:58.749 --> 16:00.500
Are you sure you are my pen pal?

242
16:00.501 --> 16:02.752
- I hope you are not lying to me. - Yes, a misunderstanding.

243
16:02.753 --> 16:04.172
What do you mean, lying?

244
16:07.633 --> 16:10.218
Prince Heinrey, why such rudeness?

245
16:10.219 --> 16:11.636
I don't believe I'm rude.

246
16:11.637 --> 16:14.055
It is Rashta who has been rude.

247
16:14.056 --> 16:16.684
I told you to be careful with your words.

248
16:17.727 --> 16:20.729
Your mistress should be equally careful with hers.

249
16:20.730 --> 16:22.105
Mistress?

250
16:22.106 --> 16:23.649
Mistress?

251
16:26.819 --> 16:30.448
Rashta did plainly tell you she was a little lost.

252
16:31.532 --> 16:34.827
Might she not have just forgotten a trivial letter?

253
16:35.620 --> 16:38.121
Heinrey explained it to her plainly.

254
16:38.122 --> 16:40.332
One could forget a letter's contents,

255
16:40.333 --> 16:43.085
but one cannot forget the very town they were born in.

256
16:47.215 --> 16:48.590
Everyone!

257
16:48.591 --> 16:52.052
Ms. Rashta claimed she was the one who exchanged letters with me,

258
16:52.053 --> 16:53.471
and I believed it was true.

259
16:54.222 --> 16:56.806
After all, a woman who is loved by His Majesty

260
16:56.807 --> 16:59.227
surely possesses a character worthy of that love.

261
16:59.810 --> 17:01.353
I believed she was trustworthy.

262
17:01.354 --> 17:04.814
Today, I wanted to speak to her about their contents,

263
17:04.815 --> 17:06.275
so we discussed them.

264
17:07.735 --> 17:09.737
And my letters were not written by her.

265
17:13.991 --> 17:15.201
A fake.

266
17:17.954 --> 17:19.371
That's enough now.

267
17:19.372 --> 17:20.373
Stop, Prince Heinrey.

268
17:20.957 --> 17:21.958
Ah…

269
17:22.917 --> 17:24.834
I would have settled this quietly.

270
17:24.835 --> 17:27.045
Your Majesty chose not to keep it private.

271
17:27.046 --> 17:30.257
Is it not considered chivalrous to defend your woman,

272
17:30.258 --> 17:32.133
more so when she's defenseless?

273
17:32.134 --> 17:34.135
If the chivalry of the Western Kingdom

274
17:34.136 --> 17:37.430
means treating a young woman so harshly over some letters

275
17:37.431 --> 17:38.974
that don't even matter…

276
17:38.975 --> 17:40.725
I wouldn't say any more on this.

277
17:40.726 --> 17:45.772
I, too, want to defend a young lady who has been unfairly misused.

278
17:45.773 --> 17:48.859
Although, of course, the one being impersonated may not be a woman,

279
17:50.319 --> 17:52.488
I might even be a man.

280
17:56.909 --> 18:00.413
How can you be so cruel? Rashta has never been a fake.

281
18:01.789 --> 18:03.665
What would be the reason for me to lie?

282
18:03.666 --> 18:05.542
It's Heinrey who won't leave it alone.

283
18:05.543 --> 18:08.170
He's trying to twist things so I look like a liar.

284
18:09.797 --> 18:12.173
Well, I think I've worked out why you're doing this.

285
18:12.174 --> 18:13.175
I think it's…

286
18:14.051 --> 18:16.177
because Rashta's not a highborn lady.

287
18:16.178 --> 18:17.888
Not refined, like you wanted.

288
18:18.639 --> 18:21.016
So you're deliberately distancing yourself.

289
18:21.017 --> 18:24.145
Was the friendship that you showed Rashta until this point all a lie?

290
18:25.187 --> 18:26.188
Is that true?

291
18:35.740 --> 18:36.991
Ms. Rashta…

292
18:43.706 --> 18:46.541
out of the countless people I have come across,

293
18:46.542 --> 18:48.544
you're by far the most brazen.

294
18:51.088 --> 18:53.798
I ask you, for the sake of our friendship,

295
18:53.799 --> 18:55.425
don't say such things, please.

296
18:55.426 --> 18:57.511
They hurt Rashta!

297
19:13.277 --> 19:15.029
I planned to remain silent.

298
19:17.156 --> 19:19.116
Misunderstandings have arisen.

299
19:19.825 --> 19:21.577
So I believe I must set them right.

300
19:22.328 --> 19:23.746
Your Majesty…

301
19:26.499 --> 19:29.959
I happen to know who wrote Prince Heinrey those letters.

302
19:29.960 --> 19:31.587
I know with whom he corresponds.

303
19:36.759 --> 19:38.594
Rashta is not that person.

304
19:48.270 --> 19:49.730
None of this is your concern.

305
19:50.731 --> 19:52.400
Just because you dislike Rashta,

306
19:53.067 --> 19:56.237
you don't need to support the prince or become involved.

307
19:56.821 --> 19:59.155
The truth must always be respected.

308
19:59.156 --> 20:02.325
It seems that Ms. Rashta can only speak the truth

309
20:02.326 --> 20:04.704
according to His Majesty the Emperor.

310
20:10.876 --> 20:12.961
It must be maddening, Your Majesty.

311
20:12.962 --> 20:13.963
What a pity.

312
20:35.735 --> 20:37.819
You've pushed this too far.

313
21:03.345 --> 21:04.722
So, Heinrey…

314
21:06.056 --> 21:08.350
for tainting my lady's reputation…

315
21:10.603 --> 21:12.021
I challenge you to a duel.

316
21:14.815 --> 21:15.816
A duel?

317
21:21.071 --> 21:22.155
Ma… Majesty!

318
21:22.156 --> 21:25.367
Get out! Get out, quickly! Move it! Get out of here!

319
21:32.541 --> 21:34.876
Shoo! Get out, now!

320
21:34.877 --> 21:36.420
I said get out!

321
21:51.727 --> 21:53.604
If I did manage to kill you,

322
21:54.522 --> 21:56.023
would I get out of here alive?

323
22:15.918 --> 22:19.171
If I would walk free, then I accept.

324
22:20.422 --> 22:21.882
Too much talk.

325
22:46.657 --> 22:48.033
Oh no!

326
24:12.034 --> 24:13.451
You're just like children.

327
24:13.452 --> 24:14.787
It's absurd!

328
24:15.287 --> 24:17.456
Do you think this behavior is justified?

329
24:20.918 --> 24:22.294
A duel?

330
24:24.004 --> 24:25.589
Oh, how foolish you must be.

331
24:27.132 --> 24:29.342
If either of you were to be killed,

332
24:29.343 --> 24:31.095
a great war would begin.

333
24:32.638 --> 24:35.391
Imagine… the pain and suffering it would cause.

334
24:35.975 --> 24:37.475
Thousands of your subjects' lives

335
24:37.476 --> 24:39.770
hang in the balance between men and their swordplay.

336
24:43.399 --> 24:45.192
Is your pride worth so much?

337
24:48.821 --> 24:50.489
Please do not forget yourself.

338
24:51.281 --> 24:53.783
I know your correspondent would not approve.

339
24:53.784 --> 24:55.452
For the sake of that friendship…

340
24:56.245 --> 24:57.246
stop this.

341
25:12.970 --> 25:14.763
It has been a memorable evening.

342
25:17.891 --> 25:20.394
I hope there's time tomorrow for us to speak again.

343
25:21.270 --> 25:23.856
So do I. I'll find a good time for us to meet.

344
25:28.110 --> 25:30.028
The most joyous aspect of this year,

345
25:30.029 --> 25:31.529
aside from the celebrations,

346
25:31.530 --> 25:33.114
is finding you, Princess.

347
25:33.115 --> 25:35.992
I agree. It looks as though we think alike.

348
25:35.993 --> 25:37.661
Here's to friendship, then.

349
25:41.790 --> 25:44.668
Do come back and have fun with Rashta again tomorrow.

350
25:56.889 --> 25:59.433
I will just wait here so I can return with His Majesty.

351
26:07.858 --> 26:08.859
Rashta.

352
26:09.902 --> 26:10.903
Yes?

353
26:21.288 --> 26:23.372
Why have you fabricated stories

354
26:23.373 --> 26:25.458
claiming that I sent gifts to you?

355
26:25.459 --> 26:26.668
What is your motivation?

356
26:27.252 --> 26:29.045
They're not fabricated.

357
26:29.046 --> 26:30.129
You know that it's true.

358
26:30.130 --> 26:32.465
Did you really think that I would play along with this?

359
26:32.466 --> 26:34.760
Rashta didn't lie about the necklace, though.

360
26:35.385 --> 26:38.430
Perhaps you have forgotten, you sent it to me as a welcome present

361
26:39.014 --> 26:40.223
for becoming mistress.

362
26:40.224 --> 26:41.849
What's all this?

363
26:41.850 --> 26:43.393
Your Majesty.

364
26:45.521 --> 26:47.815
I'm only asking about the rumors I've heard.

365
26:48.565 --> 26:51.734
In this instance, a pearl necklace that was not a gift from me.

366
26:51.735 --> 26:53.277
Did you ask Rashta personally?

367
26:53.278 --> 26:54.822
Who else should I ask, Your Majesty?

368
26:56.115 --> 26:58.783
It would be easier to merely let it pass.

369
26:58.784 --> 27:01.285
No, I'm not willing to let it pass.

370
27:01.286 --> 27:02.830
My name is being misused.

371
27:03.497 --> 27:05.123
Majesty, it wasn't me.

372
27:05.124 --> 27:06.875
I… I didn't lie.

373
27:08.710 --> 27:10.795
Do not question Rashta further.

374
27:10.796 --> 27:11.879
It is my doing.

375
27:11.880 --> 27:14.466
I was the one who sent the gift to Rashta in your name.

376
27:15.592 --> 27:18.428
Your Majesty… you sent it?

377
27:19.304 --> 27:21.390
If this really is your doing,

378
27:21.890 --> 27:23.934
may I ask Your Majesty's intentions then?

379
27:25.561 --> 27:27.562
Even if you are an emperor,

380
27:27.563 --> 27:30.691
you must not use another person's name falsely as you please.

381
27:31.775 --> 27:32.901
Is that not so?

382
27:33.402 --> 27:34.736
Your Majesty?

383
27:38.282 --> 27:40.575
Do you really have to ask these questions now?

384
27:40.576 --> 27:41.743
Yes.

385
27:42.494 --> 27:44.495
I must hold you to account

386
27:44.496 --> 27:45.747
because you have confessed.

387
27:49.251 --> 27:50.460
I'd like you to apologize now.

388
27:51.211 --> 27:52.295
You'd like what?

389
27:52.296 --> 27:54.464
I have been used quite unjustly.

390
27:55.173 --> 27:56.174
Is that so hard?

391
28:08.061 --> 28:09.438
I apologize, then.

392
28:11.857 --> 28:14.526
What you said made Rashta start spreading rumors.

393
28:15.027 --> 28:16.819
Your Majesty is accountable too.

394
28:16.820 --> 28:18.780
You should correct this false information.

395
28:20.198 --> 28:21.324
Are you serious?

396
28:21.325 --> 28:23.744
Are you worried that it could hurt your dignity?

397
28:24.745 --> 28:27.038
No matter the damage you've caused to me.

398
28:27.039 --> 28:30.042
If a necklace of pearls leaves your dignity damaged,

399
28:30.751 --> 28:33.295
then it must be as brittle as a foundation of ice.

400
28:33.962 --> 28:35.296
That could be.

401
28:35.297 --> 28:37.632
Even if that is so, it does not acquit you,

402
28:37.633 --> 28:40.551
because correcting this should be just as trivial.

403
28:40.552 --> 28:43.638
I'm asking you. Please do this with no more delay.

404
28:43.639 --> 28:46.474
This was something you should have done, Navier.

405
28:46.475 --> 28:48.851
Is making a gesture with your name so distasteful?

406
28:48.852 --> 28:50.604
Yes.

407
28:52.272 --> 28:53.899
How very narrow-minded.

408
28:54.650 --> 28:55.733
You have changed.

409
28:55.734 --> 28:57.611
Now you have heard my case.

410
29:01.782 --> 29:03.951
Give me my due respect…

411
29:04.826 --> 29:06.078
Sovieshu.

412
29:26.765 --> 29:29.934
Majesty, I'm all right, so there's nothing to worry about now.

413
29:29.935 --> 29:31.019
Let's go.

414
29:33.689 --> 29:34.731
I'm feeling tired.

415
29:36.066 --> 29:37.234
You go on your own.

416
29:58.005 --> 29:59.714
Hmm?

417
29:59.715 --> 30:00.882
Let's go.

418
30:01.550 --> 30:03.092
What has just happened?

419
30:03.093 --> 30:05.177
It sounded like a real ruckus in there earlier.

420
30:05.178 --> 30:07.513
You didn't cause any trouble, did you, Your Highness?

421
30:07.514 --> 30:08.806
No, not me. Sovieshu.

422
30:08.807 --> 30:10.266
- Sovieshu? - Sovieshu.

423
30:10.267 --> 30:11.476
- Sovieshu. - Tsk, tsk, tsk.

424
30:20.986 --> 30:22.195
Ah!

425
30:22.821 --> 30:24.947
I was so busy preparing for your party

426
30:24.948 --> 30:26.949
that I was unable to visit the palace this week.

427
30:26.950 --> 30:28.868
Good heavens!

428
30:28.869 --> 30:30.661
So you went and caused trouble?

429
30:30.662 --> 30:31.829
Why on earth did you do it?

430
30:31.830 --> 30:33.956
But it was for my party.

431
30:33.957 --> 30:36.417
I was scared no one would come and it would all be ruined.

432
30:38.045 --> 30:40.172
If it hadn't been for that Prince Heinrey…

433
30:41.590 --> 30:43.175
Should we still hold our event?

434
30:44.384 --> 30:45.385
Cancel it.

435
30:46.094 --> 30:48.512
Donate the food and gifts we bought for it in Rashta's name

436
30:48.513 --> 30:49.847
to the new home for orphans.

437
30:49.848 --> 30:51.182
And Ms. Rashta,

438
30:51.183 --> 30:53.059
the party's over for you this time.

439
30:53.060 --> 30:55.479
Banquets, outings, and games are all paused.

440
30:56.313 --> 30:57.855
You will stay in seclusion!

441
30:57.856 --> 30:58.981
Oh no!

442
30:58.982 --> 31:00.066
Not that!

443
31:01.485 --> 31:04.863
If anyone here is allowed to be upset, it should be me and not you, girl!

444
31:07.074 --> 31:11.411
You will not survive in high society if you're known for lying to people.

445
31:12.037 --> 31:13.370
Luckily for you,

446
31:13.371 --> 31:16.248
I will start the hard work needed to renew your image,

447
31:16.249 --> 31:17.750
with the aid of our allies.

448
31:17.751 --> 31:19.919
Meanwhile, hold onto His Majesty's heart…

449
31:19.920 --> 31:22.380
since it must not slip away.

450
31:23.715 --> 31:26.634
Do you know who the most fickle person here is

451
31:26.635 --> 31:27.636
in this kingdom?

452
31:28.303 --> 31:29.386
It's Sovieshu.

453
31:29.387 --> 31:32.098
That family's been fickle for generations.

454
31:32.099 --> 31:34.391
Their bloodline is all the same.

455
31:34.392 --> 31:37.561
Changeable as a weathervane blown about by the breeze.

456
31:37.562 --> 31:39.106
And insatiable too.

457
31:40.107 --> 31:41.690
All those heads…

458
31:41.691 --> 31:45.069
parted so easily from their bodies under the old king.

459
31:45.070 --> 31:46.780
So many died.

460
31:47.322 --> 31:48.573
But why were they killed?

461
31:49.032 --> 31:50.033
Were they guilty?

462
31:55.080 --> 31:56.206
Listen to me.

463
31:56.748 --> 31:58.959
Just one person can save you from all this.

464
31:59.876 --> 32:01.128
I'm that person.

465
32:03.004 --> 32:05.214
RASHTA ISHKA BOTULIN BANQUET NOTICE

466
32:05.215 --> 32:06.298
CANCELLED

467
32:09.094 --> 32:10.177
RASHTA ISHKA BOTULIN

468
32:10.178 --> 32:12.096
TREASURE HUNT EVENT

469
32:12.097 --> 32:13.890
FIND THE WAY AND CLAIM THE TREASURE!

470
32:20.355 --> 32:22.983
Maid Annie was the perpetrator, Your Majesty.

471
32:25.944 --> 32:27.320
A pity.

472
32:28.446 --> 32:30.448
I expect she gave in because of her father's debts.

473
32:31.241 --> 32:32.701
You already suspected?

474
32:33.785 --> 32:34.995
At the start,

475
32:35.745 --> 32:38.832
I only shared it because it was an amusing story.

476
32:40.041 --> 32:42.085
But when they gave me money for it…

477
32:42.836 --> 32:45.004
that's when I started to think

478
32:45.005 --> 32:47.090
that what I had done was bad.

479
32:52.929 --> 32:55.390
Her Majesty is giving you this for you to move away.

480
32:57.893 --> 32:59.351
You cannot be here.

481
32:59.352 --> 33:00.769
Hide from your father.

482
33:00.770 --> 33:02.688
Take your son and live quietly.

483
33:05.859 --> 33:08.319
The treasure lies where fire and water meet,

484
33:08.320 --> 33:10.196
and there stands a lighthouse.

485
33:10.197 --> 33:12.281
Find and bring back the two eyes

486
33:12.282 --> 33:14.618
that shine upon the world from that lighthouse.

487
33:23.251 --> 33:25.669
Those of you who picked the same animal,

488
33:25.670 --> 33:27.380
please pair up together.

489
33:36.097 --> 33:37.681
It's a dragon.

490
33:37.682 --> 33:40.184
Uh, who's got a dragon?

491
33:40.185 --> 33:41.853
Dragon over here!

492
33:42.812 --> 33:45.315
- Who could it be? - Maybe no one else has one.

493
33:58.912 --> 34:00.997
I heard you have the dragon?

494
34:03.750 --> 34:04.751
You too?

495
34:13.510 --> 34:15.344
If everyone has found their partner,

496
34:15.345 --> 34:16.679
I declare the treasure hunt…

497
34:16.680 --> 34:17.846
Open!

498
34:22.560 --> 34:24.688
I think Circe's a wonderful person.

499
34:27.899 --> 34:30.609
I'm afraid she has a difficult journey ahead.

500
34:30.610 --> 34:32.779
She will be inheriting her country's throne.

501
34:34.531 --> 34:37.826
Your Majesty, you know everything that's going on in the world.

502
34:39.869 --> 34:41.329
Shall we gallop as well?

503
34:45.166 --> 34:46.458
Hyah!

504
35:20.368 --> 35:21.953
My scarf blew off in the wind.

505
35:28.710 --> 35:29.961
Use this to secure it.

506
35:34.424 --> 35:35.800
It's one of Queen's feathers.

507
35:36.551 --> 35:37.677
It has so many uses.

508
35:38.595 --> 35:40.346
It works for sewing too.

509
35:40.347 --> 35:41.973
But also as a weapon.

510
35:43.350 --> 35:44.559
And a quill for letters.

511
35:47.312 --> 35:49.147
When you heard I was writing to you,

512
35:49.981 --> 35:51.441
I hope you weren't disappointed.

513
35:56.154 --> 35:57.656
I was overjoyed.

514
36:00.116 --> 36:02.118
Your Majesty, I'm so glad it was you.

515
36:03.578 --> 36:04.746
I really mean it.

516
36:07.582 --> 36:08.833
How did you know…

517
36:10.043 --> 36:11.378
How did you know I was the one?

518
36:12.629 --> 36:15.089
Now we shall be friends outside of the letters.

519
36:15.090 --> 36:17.966
So please, do not be a stranger, since I…

520
36:17.967 --> 36:19.427
…found you at last.

521
36:20.595 --> 36:21.888
Hmm.

522
36:23.723 --> 36:25.975
You speak of friendship outside the letters.

523
36:27.560 --> 36:28.770
That would not be easy.

524
36:30.021 --> 36:31.856
I fear troublesome eyes would soon follow.

525
36:32.816 --> 36:34.818
It's a secret between us two.

526
36:41.157 --> 36:42.951
For how long have you known…

527
36:43.743 --> 36:45.662
that I was the one writing to you?

528
36:46.746 --> 36:47.747
Hmm…

529
36:48.331 --> 36:49.833
From when I first met you.

530
36:50.625 --> 36:51.960
From that moment?

531
36:53.878 --> 36:55.547
You mean when I welcomed you?

532
36:56.339 --> 36:57.424
For that long?

533
36:58.007 --> 37:00.135
When I spotted your smiling face…

534
37:01.010 --> 37:02.429
I just knew it.

535
37:08.226 --> 37:09.602
Were you hungry?

536
37:10.603 --> 37:11.896
Was that nice?

537
37:17.152 --> 37:18.194
It's all right.

538
37:41.926 --> 37:44.763
Come to think of it, Prince Heinrey…

539
37:45.889 --> 37:47.557
He has eyes as purple as yours.

540
37:48.141 --> 37:50.185
I'm already enamored by it.

541
38:12.749 --> 38:14.501
If you don't stop looking at me,

542
38:15.043 --> 38:16.127
I think my heart will burst.

543
38:16.878 --> 38:17.879
Uh…

544
38:22.926 --> 38:24.469
You know, you resemble Queen.

545
38:26.137 --> 38:29.181
He is handsome. It's only natural.

546
38:29.182 --> 38:30.934
He's so intelligent.

547
38:31.684 --> 38:32.851
Very perceptive too.

548
38:32.852 --> 38:35.063
It's like we've always known each other.

549
38:35.605 --> 38:37.064
He truly understands…

550
38:37.065 --> 38:39.025
almost as though we're one.

551
38:41.277 --> 38:43.988
I never knew a bird could have all those expressions.

552
38:44.614 --> 38:46.658
It sounds as though you might be falling for him.

553
38:47.492 --> 38:49.660
If we were the same species…

554
38:49.661 --> 38:51.871
Hmm, we would be quite good together.

555
38:54.374 --> 38:55.833
Ah, tell me…

556
38:55.834 --> 38:58.627
Whenever I stroke his derriere,

557
38:58.628 --> 39:01.172
he wiggles and he lifts his bottom up like this.

558
39:01.756 --> 39:03.131
That must have some meaning?

559
39:03.132 --> 39:04.384
Ah…

560
39:05.051 --> 39:06.553
Mmm…

561
39:07.887 --> 39:10.055
It means "thank you," I'm certain.

562
39:10.056 --> 39:12.683
He's, uh, expressing his gratitude to you.

563
39:12.684 --> 39:14.394
Ah, is that so?

564
39:15.770 --> 39:17.355
I must do it as often as I can.

565
39:21.067 --> 39:22.569
We're nearly there, I believe.

566
39:23.236 --> 39:24.696
Will the treasure be here?

567
39:25.321 --> 39:26.906
Maybe at the end of this path?

568
39:53.683 --> 39:55.685
You said you wished to fly the skies.

569
39:57.353 --> 40:01.023
You once wrote that you wanted to soar through the clouds like a bird.

570
40:01.024 --> 40:03.776
Now you can fly just like the bird you're in love with.

571
40:06.571 --> 40:09.407
And this was the true reason that I had to find you.

572
40:10.325 --> 40:13.036
I'll show you the world as Queen perceives it.

573
40:16.998 --> 40:18.291
Are you ready?

574
40:23.254 --> 40:24.505
- Hello. - Now?

575
40:30.261 --> 40:31.971
Ready. Do it now. The sky.

576
40:35.099 --> 40:36.183
Welcome aboard.

577
40:36.184 --> 40:38.268
We are about to leave.

578
40:38.269 --> 40:40.104
Please mind the raised edge.

579
40:41.064 --> 40:42.940
And you, Your Highness,

580
40:42.941 --> 40:44.524
you mind yourself as well.

581
40:49.948 --> 40:52.492
Let's give it a go, huh? Let's do it.

582
40:56.621 --> 40:57.705
So long, then.

583
40:58.206 --> 40:59.748
Yes, yes, yes. Ah, hold on!

584
40:59.749 --> 41:01.249
Wait there!

585
41:01.250 --> 41:03.251
Wait!

586
41:03.252 --> 41:05.379
- Your picnic! Your lunch! - No, it's fine.

587
41:05.380 --> 41:07.548
Don't you want…

588
41:10.927 --> 41:12.971
Go on, go on. Now.

589
41:32.240 --> 41:33.408
May I look yet?

590
41:34.951 --> 41:36.285
Just wait another minute.

591
41:48.006 --> 41:50.674
Now, when your eyes open,

592
41:50.675 --> 41:53.427
all those matters which are tormenting you

593
41:53.428 --> 41:56.139
will feel utterly trivial and insignificant.

594
41:58.683 --> 41:59.892
Would you like to look?

595
42:01.310 --> 42:02.437
Yes.

596
42:35.303 --> 42:36.429
What do you think?

597
42:37.638 --> 42:39.264
You may shout if you want to.

598
42:39.265 --> 42:40.808
Nobody can hear you up here.

599
42:52.904 --> 42:53.905
Now louder.

600
43:24.602 --> 43:25.645
You should know…

601
43:28.439 --> 43:29.982
your messages brought such comfort.

602
43:33.528 --> 43:35.488
I was so thrilled that it was you.

603
43:41.994 --> 43:43.496
I'm so grateful.

604
44:09.230 --> 44:11.565
The closing declaration of the New Year's Ceremony

605
44:11.566 --> 44:12.567
will now be made.

606
44:27.290 --> 44:29.457
Thank you for allowing me this honor.

607
44:29.458 --> 44:30.877
I'm proud to speak.

608
44:38.301 --> 44:40.802
How marvelous our festivities were.

609
44:40.803 --> 44:43.096
What did you enjoy the most this year?

610
44:43.097 --> 44:45.891
I liked Her Majesty Empress Navier the most!

611
44:45.892 --> 44:47.059
How very kind.

612
44:52.023 --> 44:55.568
And what did I enjoy the most about the ceremony this New Year?

613
44:56.485 --> 44:59.155
The smiles and happy faces I saw everywhere.

614
44:59.739 --> 45:01.240
We were once enemies.

615
45:01.741 --> 45:02.824
But today,

616
45:02.825 --> 45:06.454
we are holding one another's hands, and we are joyous.

617
45:07.163 --> 45:09.915
We danced together and sang together as well.

618
45:09.916 --> 45:11.082
Did we not?

619
45:11.083 --> 45:12.584
Hear, hear.

620
45:12.585 --> 45:14.378
The war has ended, but…

621
45:15.504 --> 45:18.799
its aftereffects linger over our people.

622
45:19.759 --> 45:23.845
So the time has come for us to take up a new sacred fight.

623
45:23.846 --> 45:25.180
To feed the hungry,

624
45:25.181 --> 45:27.433
to clothe the poor and in need,

625
45:27.934 --> 45:30.102
and to teach our children to do better.

626
45:30.686 --> 45:32.021
I have faith in us.

627
45:33.272 --> 45:35.107
And I need you to remember this.

628
45:36.192 --> 45:39.319
That when we sheath our weapons, we are empowered.

629
45:39.320 --> 45:42.198
Our hands become free to reach out and help others.

630
45:42.823 --> 45:44.408
Let's make that our pledge…

631
45:45.034 --> 45:46.077
together.

632
45:46.744 --> 45:48.746
And may that light shine on.

633
45:51.791 --> 45:53.959
I declare, my dear friends…

634
45:53.960 --> 45:55.294
the ceremony closed.

635
46:15.982 --> 46:18.234
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS
